00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.720
Hello everyone, in this video I'm going to
show you custom automations

00:00:04.720 --> 00:00:07.400
we've done because Linear lacks this out
of the box.

00:00:08.180 --> 00:00:13.060
So in order to show it in action, let me
create Linear automation.

00:00:15.320 --> 00:00:16.180
Create issue.

00:00:18.980 --> 00:00:22.940
And a few things that we've done, which
we've had to do most of

00:00:22.940 --> 00:00:27.280
all, is that in order to move the issue to
a different stage,

00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:32.020
we usually change two things, the status
and the assignee.

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:36.360
So let's imagine that this issue is being
picked up by the developer.

00:00:37.260 --> 00:00:40.280
Like it's in progress and Dennis is
working on this.

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:45.820
And as soon as this issue is done, it
needs to be moved to the

00:00:45.820 --> 00:00:50.700
code review and the automation is supposed
to update from developer

00:00:50.700 --> 00:00:51.800
one to developer two.

00:00:53.420 --> 00:00:56.120
Like we have the following workflow that

00:00:56.120 --> 00:01:01.880
we have only two engineers for this
specific workflow.

00:01:02.060 --> 00:01:03.840
So that is why we can pre-assign this.

00:01:04.440 --> 00:01:09.200
Similarly, when we have only one QA
engineer, so that is why as soon

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:12.860
as code review is done and it's moved to
Ready for QA,

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:18.220
we know that we want to assign a
particular QA engineer to do this job.

00:01:19.220 --> 00:01:24.280
So we don't need to do this extra click
and we simply automated this.

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:29.560
And additionally, like as soon as QA is
done, as soon as

00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:34.340
it's ready for UAT, we'll update this back
to the creator of the

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:38.080
issue so they can check before it's being
released to production.

00:01:39.580 --> 00:01:43.860
And we automated another one, the labels.

00:01:43.860 --> 00:01:48.740
So as soon as it's been released, we add
the label,

00:01:49.440 --> 00:01:53.280
which will simplify my life as soon as
we're going to release this.

00:01:53.620 --> 00:01:57.400
So I'm going to gather them all and create
the release notes

00:01:57.400 --> 00:02:00.160
easier based on this label.

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:02.680
So that's it.

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:05.860
I hope it sparkles your imagination what
can be done.

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:07.300
And let me know your thoughts.
